  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146292",
      "title": "Sending Data From The Client To The API Route",
      "lectureOrder": 374,
      "videoOrder": 345,
      "sourceHash": "425f0ccb89757439d5a03df186a58e2274d8c07c100694c4837bf19e449c7888",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.653,
          "end": 4.61,
          "en": "So let's now talk to that API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.61,
          "end": 5.92,
          "en": "from our front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.92,
          "end": 9.02,
          "en": "Here we got the ContactForm and it's probably here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.02,
          "end": 12.08,
          "en": "where we wanna talk to our backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.08,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "First of all, we need to add a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 16.63,
          "en": "which is triggered when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.63,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "So I'll add a new nested function in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "the sendMessageHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 25.61,
          "en": "which will get to the default event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.61,
          "end": 28.322,
          "en": "and which should call event.preventDefault",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.322,
          "end": 30.62,
          "en": "to prevent the browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.62,
          "end": 33.36,
          "en": "where we would basically reload the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 35.88,
          "en": "because the browser automatically sends a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.88,
          "end": 37.41,
          "en": "which we don't want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.41,
          "end": 39.17,
          "en": "So prevent that default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.17,
          "end": 41.07,
          "en": "and then connect my sendMessageHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.581,
          "end": 44.663,
          "en": "to onSubmit, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.84,
          "end": 49.61,
          "en": "Now in here, we wanna send that HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.61,
          "end": 53.5,
          "en": "We wanna send that HTTP request to our API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.5,
          "end": 56.64,
          "en": "And we can do this with the good old fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.64,
          "end": 58.34,
          "en": "which is built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.34,
          "end": 62.3,
          "en": "We could also use a third party package like access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.3,
          "end": 65.292,
          "en": "Now here, we need to pass into URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.292,
          "end": 67.24,
          "en": "to which we wanna send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.24,
          "end": 70.37,
          "en": "We can omit the domain because we're using a API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.37,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "which will be hosted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 75.23,
          "en": "by the same server as our pages are hosted on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.23,
          "end": 80.005,
          "en": "So we can just add a absolute path to /API/contact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.005,
          "end": 84.18,
          "en": "/API/contact because we named the file contact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.18,
          "end": 86.303,
          "en": "in that special API folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.28,
          "end": 90.27,
          "en": "Now, we also need to pass that second argument to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.27,
          "end": 91.663,
          "en": "to configure the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.663,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "because we don't wanna use the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 97.03999999999999,
          "en": "which would be a get request with no data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.03999999999999,
          "end": 99.14,
          "en": "But instead we want to post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.14,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "with the submitted data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 104.18,
          "en": "So, set this here to post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.18,
          "end": 107.08,
          "en": "and then also add a body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.08,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "Now for the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 110.88,
          "en": "we need to extract the entered data, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 113.2,
          "en": "and we can use refs for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.2,
          "end": 115.469,
          "en": "as we did it before in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.469,
          "end": 117.8,
          "en": "or to mix things up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.8,
          "end": 120.66,
          "en": "we use state and two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.66,
          "end": 124.49,
          "en": "and I'll do the latter simply just to see this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.49,
          "end": 126.45,
          "en": "So I'll not set the body for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.45,
          "end": 129.28,
          "en": "and instead in the ContactForm component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.28,
          "end": 131.394,
          "en": "I'll now use the useState hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.394,
          "end": 134.89,
          "en": "which is imported from react to manage state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.89,
          "end": 137.59,
          "en": "for the different inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.59,
          "end": 140.25,
          "en": "initially an empty string for every input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 144.45,
          "en": "but then here we have the enteredEmail state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.45,
          "end": 146.147,
          "en": "and setEnteredEmail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.31,
          "end": 149.39,
          "en": "And I replicate this twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.39,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "to also have my entered name, state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 154.85,
          "en": "and the set entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.85,
          "end": 157.13,
          "en": "name, state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.13,
          "end": 161.803,
          "en": "and the entered message state and setEnteredMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 162.661,
          "end": 165.94,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also use one state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.94,
          "end": 169.89,
          "en": "which is an object and has a email name and message field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.89,
          "end": 170.84,
          "en": "That is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.84,
          "end": 173.263,
          "en": "And that is just standard react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 174.23,
          "end": 175.35,
          "en": "So now we've got that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "Now we need to bind this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 179.73,
          "en": "So here on this first input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.73,
          "end": 183.1,
          "en": "all now set value equal to entered email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.1,
          "end": 185.72,
          "en": "to pass the currently stored value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.72,
          "end": 188.7,
          "en": "in this state back into the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.7,
          "end": 192.47,
          "en": "but then also add the onChange prop to listen to changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.47,
          "end": 195.19,
          "en": "And here I'll add a quick inline function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.19,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "where we get the default event object automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "and then call sentEnteredEmail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.37,
          "end": 204.97,
          "en": "and set this equal to event.target.value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 204.97,
          "end": 208.79,
          "en": "That will give us access to the currently entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.79,
          "end": 212.06,
          "en": "And we can now repeat that on all the inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.06,
          "end": 216.207,
          "en": "So here on this input for the name, it's the entered name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.93,
          "end": 220.22,
          "en": "which you wanna bind and onChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.22,
          "end": 223.09,
          "en": "we wanna set the entered name therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.09,
          "end": 226.71,
          "en": "And for the text area, we can do the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.71,
          "end": 229.223,
          "en": "value is set to enteredMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.77,
          "en": "Nope, enteredMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 233.77,
          "end": 238.77,
          "en": "And we set the entered message, entered message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.8,
          "end": 241.8,
          "en": "So for text area, you also set the value prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 244.34,
          "en": "You don't add it between the text area text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.874,
          "end": 246.71,
          "en": "just to make this clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.71,
          "end": 248.7,
          "en": "So now I'm using this two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.7,
          "end": 250.9,
          "en": "to have the entered data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.9,
          "end": 254.03,
          "en": "in those state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 254.03,
          "end": 255.2,
          "en": "and therefore now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.2,
          "end": 257.09,
          "en": "when we add a body here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 257.09,
          "end": 261.15,
          "en": "to our outgoing request, we want a JSON stringify,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.15,
          "end": 263.763,
          "en": "an object with that entered data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 269.02,
          "en": "Now we can also add client side validation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.02,
          "end": 270.87,
          "en": "and simply check the entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.87,
          "end": 272.52,
          "en": "before they are submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "and possibly show an error message to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 278.6,
          "en": "But we already have some basic validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 278.6,
          "end": 281.42,
          "en": "because we added their required attribute here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.42,
          "end": 284.505,
          "en": "So that will make sure that it can't be empty anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 284.505,
          "end": 287.52,
          "en": "We should add this to the text area as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 287.52,
          "end": 289.7,
          "en": "And we already do all the validate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.7,
          "end": 291.356,
          "en": "on the server as we should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.356,
          "end": 295.505,
          "en": "And hence, I won't add another layer of validation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 295.505,
          "end": 297.62,
          "en": "But you could, because of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 297.62,
          "end": 300.86,
          "en": "with client side JavaScript based validation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.86,
          "end": 302.38,
          "en": "you have full control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.38,
          "end": 303.83,
          "en": "over which error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 303.83,
          "end": 306.01,
          "en": "you might want to show and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 306.01,
          "end": 307.47,
          "en": "but I will omit it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 307.47,
          "end": 309.65,
          "en": "It's optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 309.65,
          "end": 312.04,
          "en": "And hence here, I'll just construct the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 312.04,
          "end": 313.87,
          "en": "which will be sent to the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 313.87,
          "end": 317.03,
          "en": "and that is a object converted to JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 317.03,
          "end": 318.39,
          "en": "which has a email field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 318.39,
          "end": 320.41,
          "en": "which contains the enteredEmail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 320.41,
          "end": 323.61,
          "en": "which has a name field, which contains the enteredName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 323.61,
          "end": 325.22,
          "en": "and which has a message field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 325.22,
          "end": 327.95,
          "en": "which contains the enteredMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 327.95,
          "end": 329.12,
          "en": "And you have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 329.12,
          "end": 331.31,
          "en": "that the field names you choose here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 331.31,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "email name and message, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 335.92,
          "en": "map the field names you expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 335.92,
          "end": 339.13,
          "en": "in your API route function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 339.13,
          "end": 342.51,
          "en": "Here, I'm trying to extract email, name and message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 342.51,
          "end": 346.61,
          "en": "So these should be the identifiers I set here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 346.61,
          "end": 348.423,
          "en": "email, name and message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 350.08,
          "end": 351.63,
          "en": "With that resetting this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 351.63,
          "end": 352.65,
          "en": "last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 352.65,
          "end": 354.76,
          "en": "I'll also add a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 354.76,
          "end": 359.58,
          "en": "and set the content type header to application JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 359.58,
          "end": 361.08,
          "en": "to make the backend aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 361.08,
          "end": 364.52,
          "en": "of the fact that this request will carry JSON data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 364.52,
          "end": 367.513,
          "en": "and hence it can be parsed correctly by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 368.57,
          "end": 370.63,
          "en": "This now sends the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 370.63,
          "end": 372.21,
          "en": "We're not doing anything else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 372.21,
          "end": 374.27,
          "en": "not working with the response,",
          "zh": ""
